   "evidence": "The current proof already routes through the dual: lines 51-57 build `variance_dual_stdGaussian (innerSL \u211d v)`, rewrite with `innerSL_apply_norm`, then undo the functional with `rw [innerSL_apply_apply, real_inner_comm v x]`. Lines 67-71 of `integral_norm_sq_stdGaussian` repeat that same `innerSL_apply_apply`/`real_inner_comm` conversion to reach `IsGaussian.integrable_dual_sq (stdGaussian E) (innerSL \u211d (b i))` \u2014 the conversion exists only because the dual-level statement is missing. `variance_of_integral_eq_zero` is upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Probability/Moments/Variance.lean:174 and `innerSL_apply_norm` is upstream/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/InnerProductSpace/LinearMap.lean:225.",
